UPDALL(1)

# Name

updall - simple update utility

# SYNOPSIS

updall [...FLAGS]

# DESCRIPTION

The updall command reads a list of entries from its configuration file,
runs their update scripts in order, then runs their cleanup scripts in order
once updates are finished.

# FLAGS

|[ -h
:[ --help
:[
:< Show help and exit.
|  -V
:  --version
:[
:  Show version and exit.
|  -v
:  --verbose
:[
:  Output debug info to stderr (repeatable).
|  -c
:  --config-file
:  _FILE_
:  Alternate location of the config file.
|  -d
:  --disable
:  _ENTRY_
:  Disable an entry by name (repeatable).
|  -n
:  --dry-run
:[
:  Only print which updaters would run.


# SEE ALSO

_updall_(5)
